+---
+id: task-002-availability-query-for-rental-service
+type: task
+title: "Availability query for rental service"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is
+optional. It returns the ids of the equipment of that kind, or of any kind when none is given, that is
+free for the whole period, sorted. The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented.
+
+## Done
+
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: 12 tests for `availability`, written first and seen failing (10 failing, the two
+  throw cases passing only because the method was missing), then passing against the implementation. They
+  cover all and per-kind listing, sorting, an empty catalogue, half-open back-to-back periods, several
+  bookings of one item, isolation between items, quotes not changing the result, and invalid kind and
+  period.
+- `src/index.ts`: `availability` and the `AvailabilityQuery` type, with doc comments. The overlap rule and
+  the period parsing moved into the helpers `isFree` and `parsePeriod`, shared with `book` and `quote`, and
+  the kind check moved into `assertKind`, shared with `addEquipment`. Behaviour of the existing methods is
+  unchanged; their 24 tests still pass.
+- `README.md`: a bullet describing `availability`.
+- Design choices are recorded in `dl-005`.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `npm test` (`node --test`): 36 of 36 pass.
+- `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` with a temporary TypeScript 5 install outside the project: no errors.
+
+## Open points
+
+- Sorting uses plain string comparison, so `board-10` lists before `board-2`. Recorded in `dl-005`.
+- A listed id is not a reservation: a booking made after the query can take it. `book` remains the check.
